Q: How to make an entire edge of a div resizable? A: <p>Create a custom <code>.handler</code> child element that has <strong>Pointer Events</strong> attached, to make it work for both touch screens and mouse (Mobile and desktop).<br />
The following example uses Event delegation, so it'll work even for dynamically generated elements:</p>
<p><div class="snippet" data-lang="js" data-hide="false" data-console="true" data-babel="false" data-babel-preset-react="false" data-babel-preset-ts="false">
<div class="snippet-code">
<pre class="snippet-code-js lang-js prettyprint-override"><code>const handleResizerDown = (ev) =&gt; {
  const elResizer = ev.target.closest(".resizer");
  if (!elResizer) return;
  elResizer.setPointerCapture(ev.pointerId);
};

const handleResizerMove = (ev) =&gt; {
  const elResizer = ev.target;
  if (!elResizer.hasPointerCapture(ev.pointerId)) return;
  const elParent = elResizer.parentElement;
  const w = elParent.getBoundingClientRect().width;
  elParent.style.width = `${w + ev.movementX}px`; 
};

addEventListener("pointerdown", handleResizerDown);
addEventListener("pointermove", handleResizerMove);</code></pre>
<pre class="snippet-code-css lang-css prettyprint-override"><code>:has(&gt;.resizer) {
  box-sizing: border-box;
  position: relative;
  overflow: hidden;
  min-width: 2em;
  background: #eee;
  padding: 2rem;

  .resizer {
    position: absolute;
    z-index: 1;
    width: 10px;
    height: 100%;
    right: 0px;
    top: 0;
    background: #0bf;
    cursor: col-resize;
    touch-action: none;
  }
}</code></pre>
<pre class="snippet-code-html lang-html prettyprint-override"><code>&lt;div&gt;
  &lt;div&gt;
    Resizable (horizontally)&lt;br&gt;
        Lorem ipsum dolor sit amet, consectetur adipisicing elit. Numquam consequuntur praesentium alias deserunt quas! Ex unde, aperiam sunt quae asperiores fugiat aspernatur eligendi amet. Iste molestias facilis, porro quos eius?
  &lt;/div&gt;
  &lt;div class="resizer"&gt;&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;</code></pre>
</div>
</div>
</p>
<p>If you want to create split views you could use this <strong><a href="https://github.com/rokobuljan/split-view" rel="nofollow noreferrer">Split-View script</a></strong> <em>(for full disclosure: I am the author)</em></p>
