Q: c++20 concepts: how to requires a class with specific name of static function A: <p>This line checks if <code>require_static_function_name&lt;MyClass&gt;</code> is valid or not:</p>
<pre class="lang-cpp prettyprint-override"><code>bool has_static = requires { require_static_function_name&lt;MyClass&gt;;};
</code></pre>
<p>As long as there's a definition of <code>MyClass</code>, it will be <code>true</code>. If there is no <code>MyClass</code>, it'll fail to compile.</p>
<p>What you want is to get the result of the actual <code>require_static_function_name&lt;MyClass&gt;</code> expression:</p>
<pre class="lang-cpp prettyprint-override"><code>bool has_static = require_static_function_name&lt;MyClass&gt;;
</code></pre>
<p><a href="https://godbolt.org/z/j7E1rWc34" rel="nofollow noreferrer">Demo</a></p>
<hr />
<p>A stricter test for different overloads of <code>something</code> would be to take the address of the <code>static</code> member function in the concept. This would not allow for <code>args...</code> to be implicitly converted etc.:</p>
<pre class="lang-cpp prettyprint-override"><code>template &lt;class T, class Ret, class... Args&gt;
concept require_static_function_name = requires {
    static_cast&lt;Ret(*)(Args...)&gt;(&amp;T::something);
};
</code></pre>
<p>Using it would be mostly the same as before, except you add the return type too:</p>
<pre class="lang-cpp prettyprint-override"><code>bool has_static = require_static_function_name&lt;MyClass, void&gt;;
</code></pre>

Q: How to call the methods of one model class inside another model class A: <p>Sometimes is useful to have in your controllers something like:</p>

<pre><code>public function __construct(){

    $this-&gt;CI =&amp; get_instance();
}
</code></pre>

<p>So, when you need another model you can do:</p>

<pre><code>$this-&gt;CI-&gt;load-&gt;model('another_codeigniter_model_name', 'another');
$something = $this-&gt;CI-&gt;another-&gt;com_fun();
</code></pre>
